# diff-kernels' known differences: `<name> <max ulps | any> <reason>`.
# A name is a std_kernels function (or a gm function, for the math swap)
# whose answer differs from the old one; `any` is a difference that is not
# a number of ulps (NaN against a number, a sign, a text). A line whose name
# agrees fails the run: remove it.
#
# Not here: the gm -> Gompute 2.0 swap's differences (cosh, sinh, log10 and
# the kernels, folds and Ac family over them). The f128 reference judges each
# (kernels/reference.zig): Gompute stays within its documented bound on every
# input and its worst case is no farther than gm's, so diff-kernels prints
# them as old-side bugs instead.
